  "configuration_id": "config_048",
  "reason": "The current best is config_022 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.678). The image encoder comparison (resnet50 vs imagenet_vit_l) was previously tested only with pca_n2000 (config_003: 0.639 vs config_051: 0.635), yielding a near-tie. However, with the stronger learned scvi_n200 RNA representation, the interaction with the image encoder may differ—ViT-L's richer spatial features could complement scvi's latent embeddings more effectively than ResNet50's. config_048 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) is the cleanest single-variable extension of the current best, isolating the image encoder upgrade while keeping the proven optimal aggregation (avgpool) and fusion (weighted). This is the highest-value test: if it improves, it gives a stronger baseline for the final 2 experiments; if not, it confirms ResNet50 suffices and redirects remaining budget to other axes. Expected cost is ~7-8 GPU hours (comparable to config_051 at 7.02), which is moderate and leaves ample budget for the remaining two experiments."
}

